<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIAN NOON RADIO HEADLINES-JULY 31.</title>
<headline>ESTONIAN NOON RADIO HEADLINES-JULY 31.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the headlines on Kuku Raadio at noon. Reuters has not verified these reports and does not vouch for their accuracy:</p>
<p>- Five years ago today Erika Salumae won the first Olympic gold for Estonia since the restoration of independence.</p>
<p>- Joining the European Union will mean an increase in the number of bureaucrats, the minister responsible for regional affairs said.</p>
<p>- A man who shot a bear without a permit was charged by the police.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom, +372 620 9202, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
